    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 537\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 7002-B, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  agriculture and markets law and the public\n      lands law, in relation to access to viable agricultural  land  for\n      new and beginning farmers\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This  bill  would  require  the  Department of Agriculture and Markets\n(DAM) to implement measures to help promote the transfer of viable agri-\ncultural land from existing owners to new farmers  and,  in  cooperation\nwith  the  Office of General Services, to develop an inventory of State-\nowned public land that may be viable for farming and make such  informa-\ntion available on its website.\n\n  My  administration is committed to supporting our State's farmers. For\nexample, DAM has established a Beginning Farmer Working Group, which has\nbegun examining a broad  range  of  issues  important  to  new  farmers,\nincluding  access  to  viable  farm land. In addition, the Enacted State\nBudget for 2014-2015 included funding for the Beginning Farmer  NY  Fund\nto provide grants to beginning farmers, as well as student loan forgive-\nness  for agricultural college graduates who commit to farm in New York.\nThis bill, however, would impose substantial, unbudgeted  costs  on  the\nState  and,  as  such, would be better addressed during the annual State\nBudget negotiations.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 537,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2014
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
